  "description": "M6. Extends story_gen4_legendary_accept's verified 46-action route, which ends with a two-member team whose slot 0 holds charcoal and a three-item bag. Equips choice_band onto slot 1 through the item bar's own overlay entry point (openItemEquipModal(item, {fromBagIdx}), bundle.deobfuscated.js:64857) so that BOTH members are holding, then hands slot 0's item off to slot 1 (the [data-idx] row at 79541-79545). That both-holding case is the one that distinguishes the hand-off from an unequip followed by an equip: the source gives the target's old item to the SOURCE member, where unequip+equip would route it to the bag. Finally unequips slot 0 (#btn-equip-to-bag with fromPokemonIdx >= 0, 79549-79553). The final action removes slot 1's item through the OTHER spelling of the same exit -- the holder row's own [data-unequip] button (79521-79531), which the M6 brief cites -- so the scenario proves both spellings land on the same engine action on both runtimes.",
